Speed-bound investigation (claudebox-S521)

(3) Fast-runner bound for n=4: v3 < 1/|I(v1,v2)|, |I|=largest common-safe window.
      (v1,v2)      |I|  v3 must be <
       (1, 2)      1/8           8.0
       (1, 3)      1/6           6.0
       (3, 5)     1/10          10.0
       (7, 9)     1/18          18.0
     (11, 13)     1/26          26.0

   min largest-window over coprime slow pairs with speeds<=S (=> bound on v3):
     slow<=   5: min|I|=0.0875  => v3 < 11.4  (~2*S: ratio bound)
     slow<=  10: min|I|=0.0472  => v3 < 21.2  (~2*S: ratio bound)
     slow<=  20: min|I|=0.0243  => v3 < 41.1  (~2*S: ratio bound)
     slow<=  40: min|I|=0.0123  => v3 < 81.0  (~2*S: ratio bound)

   GAP: some slow pairs have EMPTY common window (bad sets tile) -> no bound;
   that casework is why B(n) is large and the recursion does not close trivially.

(1)+(2): with bound B, modulus Q~ln B, check over speeds<lcm(2..Q)~B (~B^(n-1) sets).
   So B(n) is the whole bottleneck.  Status: B(n) explicit but super-exponential;
   LRC proven for n<=7 by such inductive interval arguments; n=14 far beyond reach.
